ROOT CAUSE FIXED (real product defect, found by live probe, not by guessing):
  ruke_ml/workers/runner.py:_stdin_reader(q) took a queue argument but main() started the
  thread WITHOUT args=(q,) -> TypeError in the thread -> the worker's only control channel
  died at startup -> every spawned worker stayed alive and silent until its deadline
  (default 900 s), which is what hung tests/test_supervisor_workers.py for >4.5 minutes.
MECHANISM FIXES (not per-example):
  1. _stdin_reader runs wrapped and announces {"kind":"control_channel_failed"} on stdout,
     so a broken control loop is a fast typed failure instead of a silent hang.
  2. Worker emits a {"kind":"ready","capability","pid","schema_version"} handshake; the pool
     waits for it (LIMITS.worker_ready_timeout_s) before trusting a child with a job.
  3. Pool matches job_id and ignores progress/ready/foreign lines: an answer for another job
     is never misfiled as this job's result.
  4. {"kind":"shutdown"} control: idle-TTL and supervisor teardown now exit cleanly instead of
     always escalating to terminate/kill (about 10 s per worker before).
  5. Worker stderr is captured (bounded 8 KB) instead of DEVNULL; DEVNULL hid the very traceback
     that explained the hang.
  6. contracts.ERROR_REASONS was missing "evaluation_required" while 8 call sites raised it, so
     every such honest failure was converted into reason="internal". Added, plus a package scan
     guard test that rejects any reason literal the contract itself would refuse.
  7. CAPABILITIES advertised "video.observations" with no worker handler -> routed to the timeline
     observations path (capability name fixes the op so it cannot silently rewrite a baseline).
     Guard test: every declared capability must reach a handler and vice versa.
  8. security.egress_blocked_for_workers was dead code: never applied to a real child. Now every
     spawned capability worker gets RUKE_EGRESS=blocked / proxy sink / HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1.
  9. child_env now creates and exports RUKE_SCRATCH_DIR (children start without ensure_dirs()).
 10. lifecycle._popen is the single spawn seam (testable without monkeypatching stdlib).
TEST-SIDE: RpcRoundTrip and OwnedWorkers now lower LIMITS.worker_deadline_s / worker_ready_timeout_s
  / terminate_grace_s for the duration of the class (restored in teardown) so a broken helper can
  never wedge the suite for the production 15-minute deadline again.
